WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.550
January and June do not merely
contain different error magnitudes.

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:07.910
They occupy different positions
in the forecast timeline.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:13.580
The daily plot keeps that order and shows
mostly larger negative residuals later in

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:14.670
the validation period.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:18.790
We summarize each date using
its actual recorded hours,

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.510
then form Monday starting weekly groups.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.570
There are twenty seven such groups,

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:27.030
with counts ranging from twenty
three to one hundred and sixty eight.

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.970
Partial boundary weeks remain partial.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:34.720
We have not shuffled observations or
invented missing targets to make every day

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:36.570
and week look equally complete.

00:00:38.692 --> 00:00:43.222
The validation window contains
ten unrecorded hourly slots.

00:00:43.932 --> 00:00:49.452
A row after a gap must not be treated
as exactly one hour after the row before

00:00:49.452 --> 00:00:50.082
it.

00:00:50.452 --> 00:00:53.642
The pair builder therefore
compares timestamps,

00:00:53.712 --> 00:00:56.102
retaining only differences of one hour.

00:00:56.572 --> 00:01:01.402
It finds four thousand, three hundred
and forty six consecutive hour pairs.

00:01:01.872 --> 00:01:07.062
For these pairs, the residual correlation
is about zero point eight six eight.

00:01:07.772 --> 00:01:12.832
The full function guards against too few
pairs and zero variation before computing

00:01:12.832 --> 00:01:13.522
correlation.

00:01:14.312 --> 00:01:16.422
Missing slots remain missing;

00:01:17.392 --> 00:01:22.432
inserting zero outcomes would alter both
the evaluation population and its apparent

00:01:22.432 --> 00:01:23.502
time structure.

00:01:25.692 --> 00:01:30.132
A strong positive correlation says
neighboring residuals tend to move

00:01:30.132 --> 00:01:32.182
together in these observed pairs.

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:35.422
It does not prove a cause
or guarantee persistence.

00:01:36.292 --> 00:01:41.375
Weekly mean absolute error ranges from
thirty two point seven five to one hundred

00:01:41.375 --> 00:01:44.362
and fifty seven point two
six on the observed weeks.

00:01:44.892 --> 00:01:48.462
That range is descriptive,
not a confidence interval for next week.

00:01:49.032 --> 00:01:54.312
The earlier forest seed standard deviation
near zero point zero five five has another

00:01:54.312 --> 00:01:54.982
meaning.

00:01:55.372 --> 00:01:58.942
It measures fitting variation
on the same validation dates.

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:02.662
Repeating seeds does not
produce new future periods.

00:02:03.292 --> 00:02:07.472
We retain those distinctions instead
of reporting an unsupported independent

00:02:07.472 --> 00:02:08.982
observation interval.

00:02:11.192 --> 00:02:15.082
To inspect the level difference,
first match month,

00:02:15.252 --> 00:02:18.322
hour and working day cells
between the two years.

00:02:18.852 --> 00:02:20.062
Within each cell,

00:02:20.152 --> 00:02:24.752
calculate a historical mean from January
through June twenty eleven training

00:02:24.752 --> 00:02:25.402
targets.

00:02:26.032 --> 00:02:31.572
Weight that old cell mean by the number
of later validation rows belonging to the

00:02:31.572 --> 00:02:32.062
cell.

00:02:32.432 --> 00:02:37.952
This asks what the old within cell
levels look like under the later calendar

00:02:37.952 --> 00:02:38.922
composition.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:40.545
All four thousand,

00:02:40.545 --> 00:02:45.662
three hundred and fifty seven validation
observations find a historical cell,

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:47.342
with none dropped as unmatched.

00:02:48.092 --> 00:02:50.982
The weighting changes
composition for this diagnostic,

00:02:51.512 --> 00:02:55.202
while the previously fitted
candidate itself remains unchanged.

00:02:57.317 --> 00:03:01.968
The reweighted historical cell means
average one hundred and twenty one point

00:03:01.968 --> 00:03:04.347
three one rentals per hour.

00:03:04.957 --> 00:03:08.827
The later observed mean is two
hundred and fifteen point two zero.

00:03:09.697 --> 00:03:13.267
Their difference is about
ninety three point eight nine.

00:03:13.857 --> 00:03:18.671
This is distinct from the selected group
predictions mean of one hundred and forty

00:03:18.671 --> 00:03:19.917
two point eight six,

00:03:19.917 --> 00:03:25.557
because the diagnostic conditions on month
too and uses only matching first half

00:03:25.557 --> 00:03:26.787
historical cells.

00:03:27.097 --> 00:03:29.787
It is not a newly ranked
forecasting candidate.

00:03:30.257 --> 00:03:34.857
Its role is to make an observed level
difference easier to inspect after

00:03:34.857 --> 00:03:36.647
outcomes have become available.

00:03:38.957 --> 00:03:39.837
Matching month,

00:03:39.837 --> 00:03:45.017
hour and day type makes a calendar
composition only explanation less

00:03:45.017 --> 00:03:49.487
adequate, because a substantial difference
remains within those shared cells.

00:03:50.117 --> 00:03:53.867
It does not identify which real
world cause produced that difference.

00:03:54.497 --> 00:03:58.307
Demand growth, unmodelled weather
or other changes could contribute.

00:03:58.917 --> 00:04:02.017
We have not measured their separate
effects or carried out a causal

00:04:02.017 --> 00:04:02.767
intervention.

00:04:03.357 --> 00:04:06.107
If a different later mix were observed,

00:04:06.437 --> 00:04:10.507
its weights and diagnostic could change
even with the same historical means.

00:04:11.037 --> 00:04:14.987
That is why the weights,
unmatched count and scope are saved,

00:04:15.157 --> 00:04:19.597
and why this picture does not silently
authorize refitting or changing the frozen

00:04:19.597 --> 00:04:20.247
split.

